title: Food Shortages
subtitle: Hunger reigns in the cities...
new-page: true
view-if: hunger >= 25 and food_shortages_timer = 0 and year != 1917
tags: event
on-arrival: {!
  Q.food_shortages_timer += 8;
  Q.workers_none += 2; 
  Q.workers_b -= 4; Q.middle_b -= 2; Q.intelligentsia_b -= 2
  Q.workers_unrest += 5; Q.middle_unrest += 2; Q.intelligentsia_unrest += 2;
  if (Q.crime < 50) { Q.crime_rate += 3; }
  Q.instability += 0.5; Q.disillusionment += 0.1;

  if (Q.m_in_gov != 1) {
    Q.workers_left_m += 1; Q.workers_m += 1; Q.workers_right_m += 1; 
    Q.middle_left_m += 0.5; Q.middle_m += 0.5; Q.middle_right_m += 1; 
  } else {
    Q.workers_left_m += 0.5; Q.workers_m += 0.5; Q.workers_right_m += 0.5;
  }
  if (Q.lsr_in_gov != 1) {
    Q.workers_lsr += 1;
  } else {
    Q.workers_lsr += 0.5;
  }
!}

= Food Shortages

The cities are wracked by hunger. Rationing and bread lines become a constant feature of urban life, with little sign of improvement. 

Workers are beginning to wonder: if the revolution does not solve the issue of bread, then what was it even for?

- @increase_rations
- @agitate
- @reserves
- @increase_price
- @nothing

@increase_rations
title: Issue emergency rations in the cities to offset shortages. 
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: -1 resources
unavailable-subtitle: -1 resources – We lack the resources. 
on-arrival: {!
  Q.resources -= 1;
  Q.workers_b += 4*(1-Q.b_dissent); 
  Q.workers_unrest -= 5; 
!}

We use government resources to purchase grain directly from the peasants, and issue a round of emergency rations. These are at best temporary measures, however.

@agitate
title: We must agitate against the bourgeois speculators who are sabotaging the grain supply! 
on-arrival: {!
  Q.workers_b += 2*(1-Q.b_dissent); 
  Q.instability += 0.5;
  Q.workers_unrest -= 3; Q.peasants_unrest += 2; Q.kulaks_unrest += 4; Q.middle_unrest += 2;
!}

We publish articles and make speeches blaming the crisis on various counterrevolutionary forces. Although this redirects some of the anger, there are limits to how far propaganda can shield us. 

@reserves 
title: Open our urban reserves to increase the supply in the cities. 
choose-if: urban_stockpile > 0 
unavailable-subtitle: The urban stockpiles are drained. 
on-arrival: {!
  Q.urban_stockpile_release += 0.2; 
  Q.workers_b += 2*(1-Q.b_dissent); 
  Q.workers_unrest -= 3;
!}

We use our reserves to offset some of the shortages in the cities, although this is at best a temporary concession if the underlying problem is not addressed. 


@increase_price
title: Increase the price of grain paid out to peasant producers.
subtitle: -1 resources 
choose-if: resources >= 1 
on-arrival: resouces -= 1 
go-to: food_policy.increase_price

@nothing
title: There's nothing we can do. 
on-arrival: {!
  Q.workers_unrest += 4;
  Q.workers_b -= 2; 
!}
go-to: root
